.TH ENRICH.PY 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
enrich.py \- the @enrich lane: add NVD, EPSS and CISA KEV context to CVEs and assign Sev5\(enSev1
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B enrich.py
.BI \-\-report " FILE"
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-no\-db ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-nvd ]
.br
.B enrich.py
.BI \-\-cves " LIST"
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-no\-db ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-nvd ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent enrich.py
.I options
.br
.B python3 $FLEET_CODE/lanes/enrich.py
.I options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B enrich.py
takes the CVEs the Go agent found, or an explicit list, adds the context that
decides whether anyone should care, and writes one JSON file that
.BR brief.py (1)
renders and
.BR cti\-jira (1)
and
.BR cti\-kev (1)
read. It is run by
.BR run\-digest (1)
on every daily digest, between the mailbox ingest and the render.
.PP
For each CVE it fetches:
.TP
.B NVD 2.0
CVSS base score and severity (v3.1, else v3.0, else v2, preferring the
score NVD itself assigned over the CNA's), the English description (first
400 characters), status, publication date and NVD's own KEV flag. One
request per CVE, spaced 6.5 seconds apart without an API key and 0.7
seconds with one. Results are cached for 7 days.
.TP
.B FIRST EPSS
The probability of exploitation in the next 30 days and its percentile, in
batches of 100.
.TP
.B CISA KEV
The whole catalog, cached for 12 hours: date added, remediation due date,
known ransomware use, name and required action. When the catalog cannot be
fetched, NVD's flag decides KEV membership, but no due date is known.
.PP
A request that is refused with HTTP 403, 429 or 503 is retried after 15 and
then 30 seconds; any other failure after 5 and 10 seconds. A source that
still does not answer is listed under
.B degraded
in the output, and the digest prints a DEGRADED banner; it never stops the
run.
.PP
Then every finding gets a band. Presence comes only from the scanner
.RB ( status
.B PRESENT
with a host count above zero); this lane never decides it.
.I Exploited
means on KEV or EPSS at least 10%.
.TP
.B Sev5
Present and exploited.
.TP
.B Sev4
Present, not known to be exploited, whatever its CVSS.
.TP
.B Sev3
Status
.B UNKNOWN
(the scanner had no mapping) and on KEV or EPSS at least 50%.
.TP
.B Sev2
Exploited but not present (including UNKNOWN with EPSS from 10% to under
50%), or UNKNOWN with CVSS 9.0 or more.
.TP
.B Sev1
Everything else.
.PP
Each finding also gets a
.B rationale
(the KEV deadline when the CVE is present, EPSS, CVSS, presence, ransomware
use),
.B kev_days_left
(negative when overdue), and
.B is_new
and
.BR first_seen ,
read from
.I memory.db
before the upsert: true when the findings table has never seen the CVE,
null when there is no database to ask. Within a band, findings are sorted
by host count, then days overdue, then EPSS.
.PP
The output also carries the band counts,
.BR kev_deadlines
(overdue, due within 14 days, worst overdue, ransomware, counted over
present findings only), the report's header facts, the list of email
subjects the ingest read, and the novelty totals. A run with no CVEs still
writes a result, so the digest still goes out.
.PP
Unless
.B \-\-no\-db
is given and there is at least one finding, every row is then upserted into
.I memory.db
by running
.B fleet\-db finding upsert
with the same Python interpreter. A failed upsert is logged; the JSON is
already written. When
.B fleet\-db
cannot be found, a WARNING names every path tried.
.PP
.B enrich.py
sends no mail and does not read the mailbox or the scanner. Progress goes to
standard error, prefixed
.BR [enrich] .
.SH OPTIONS
Exactly one of
.B \-\-report
and
.B \-\-cves
is required, and
.B \-\-out
always is.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " FILE"
The Go agent's markdown report. Table rows whose first cell is a CVE ID and
that have at least 8 cells are read as CVE, status, provider, QIDs, host
count, score, last seen, sample hosts and the scanner's reason; in the older
8-column layout the last cell is taken as hosts when the host count is above
zero and as the reason otherwise. The header facts (mailbox, lookback,
email counts, provider, generated) and the
.B "## Emails read this run"
table are carried into the output.
.TP
.BI \-\-cves " LIST"
Comma-separated CVE IDs, for the scout lane. Each is scored with status
.BR UNKNOWN ,
provider
.B scout
and no hosts. Entries that are not CVE IDs are dropped without comment.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Where to write the JSON. Missing directories are created.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-db
Do not upsert into
.IR memory.db .
Novelty is still read from it if it exists.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-nvd
Do not query NVD: EPSS and KEV only, much faster. Findings have no CVSS or
description, and NVD is not reported as degraded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B enrich.py
reads only its process environment and does not load
.I fleet.env
itself.
.B run\-digest
sources it first, and so does
.B sudo cti\-agent enrich.py
(the wrapper loads it), so
.B NVD_API_KEY
and
.B FLEET_USER_AGENT
from
.I fleet.env
apply to a hand run too. Run directly, without the wrapper, they are unset
unless exported.
.TP
.B NVD_API_KEY
NVD API key, sent as the
.B apiKey
header. Unset: 6.5 seconds between NVD requests instead of 0.7, roughly
ten times slower.
.I fleet.env
section 6, ENRICHMENT.
.TP
.B FLEET_USER_AGENT
User-Agent sent to NVD, EPSS and CISA.
Default:\~\fB\%cti\-agent\-enrich/1.0\fR. Section 6.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
State directory: the caches and
.I memory.db
are under
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state .
Default:\~\fI~/fleet\fR. Section 3, PATHS; set by the units and the wrapper.
.TP
.B FLEET_CODE
Where
.B bin/fleet\-db
is looked for first, then
.IR $FLEET_HOME/bin/fleet\-db ,
then the
.I bin
directory beside this lane's own
.IR lanes .
Set by the units and the wrapper.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/raw\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.md
The Go agent's report, the usual
.BR \-\-report .
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json
The daily's
.BR \-\-out ,
written by
.BR run\-digest .
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/nvd\-cache.json
NVD results, trusted for 7 days, rewritten whenever a CVE was fetched.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/kev\-cache.json
The KEV catalog, trusted for 12 hours. Delete either cache to force a
refetch.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/memory.db
Read for novelty (read-only), written through
.BR fleet\-db (1).
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/bin/fleet\-db
The upsert helper.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The JSON was written, including when sources were degraded, there were no
CVEs, or the database upsert failed or was skipped.
.TP
.B 1
The report could not be read or the output could not be written (Python
traceback).
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments: neither or both of
.B \-\-report
and
.BR \-\-cves ,
or no
.BR \-\-out .
.SH EXAMPLES
Re-enrich today's report without touching the findings database:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent enrich.py \-\-no\-db \e
  \-\-report /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/raw\-$(date +%F).md \e
  \-\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-test.json
.EE
.PP
Score two CVEs quickly, without NVD:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent enrich.py \-\-skip\-nvd \-\-no\-db \e
  \-\-cves CVE\-2026\-1234,CVE\-2026\-5678 \e
  \-\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-test.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brief.py (1),
.BR scout.py (1),
.BR fleet\-db (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-kev (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 3; fleet\-kit/README.md, "Why Sev5\(enSev1 instead of
CVSS" and "CISA KEV remediation deadlines".
